From 96401c6a24d1aadf7e80a11cd6d0a60e2cec05cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 10:28:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] transports: tenant VK + team create accept rate_limit /
 budgets / provider_configs

The v1 tenant CRUD bodies (CreateTenantVirtualKeyRequest +
CreateTenantTeamRequest) were name-and-description only.  Anything
else in the payload silently dropped, so the resulting VKs had
empty provider_configs and bifrost's catalog auto-resolve sent every
/v1 call to whichever global provider claimed the model.  That bypass
left logs unstamped (no tenant_id on the request ctx) and the
dashboard's tenant_id-filtered logs view empty.

Extend the bodies to the legacy create shape:

  VK:
    rate_limit       *CreateRateLimitRequest
    budgets          []CreateBudgetRequest
    provider_configs []{provider, weight?, allowed_models}

  Team:
    rate_limit       *CreateRateLimitRequest
    budgets          []CreateBudgetRequest
    calendar_aligned bool

provider_configs entries are validated against the tenant's provider
set (via configStore.GetProvidersConfigByTenant); unknown providers
get a 400 instead of silently breaking routing later.  Owned
rate_limit / budgets get pinned to tenant_id through the existing
ForTenant configstore methods, so cross-tenant lookups stay scoped.

Backward compat: when none of the new fields are present, both
handlers take the original direct-create path (no transaction) so
existing stub-store happy-path tests keep passing.  Rich-path tests
exercise the new code via a stubbed ExecuteTransaction + per-row
recorders.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
